# Persian RTL Chat Responses

When the user communicates in Persian, or when the assistant reply includes Persian content, render **everything Persian** RTL — paragraphs, headings, lists, tables, and blockquotes. **Only code blocks stay LTR.** This single LTR exception wins over every other rule.

## Mandatory trigger (every chat, every turn)

Apply RTL formatting **on every assistant turn** in **every chat session** when **any** of these is true:

1. The **user message** is in Persian (or mixed with Persian).
2. The **assistant reply** includes Persian prose — headings, bullets, explanations, summaries, troubleshooting steps, even if the topic is technical (server, 502, PHP-FPM, Livewire, deploy).
3. The user **explicitly asks** for RTL / Persian formatting (e.g. «همیشه RTL»).

**No carve-out** for “technical”, “debug”, “ops”, or “English-heavy” replies: if the body contains Persian sentences or Persian headings/lists, those parts **must** use `<div dir="rtl">` per this file. Do **not** ship bare LTR `###` / `-` Persian lines because the answer is about infrastructure.

**English-only replies / English-only plans** (zero Persian prose) → no RTL wrappers.

## Scope (non-negotiable)

Apply this rule to **all** of the following when the content is Persian (or mixed with Persian prose):

- Assistant **chat replies** — including follow-ups, re-summaries, and “repeat last answer in RTL” requests
- **Plan mode** plans (`CreatePlan` body and plan `.md` files shown to the user)
- Plan iterations / plan updates written back into the plan document

Do **not** apply to: app UI, lang files, Filament copy, or English-only technical replies.

**English-only replies / English-only plans** → no RTL wrappers.

## Why code sometimes turns RTL (root cause)

If a `<div dir="rtl">` is **not properly closed in markdown's view**, every block after it — including code blocks — inherits RTL. A div fails to close when there is **no blank line immediately inside it**. Markdown then treats the following content as raw HTML inside the still-open div, so the code becomes right-aligned.

**The fix is mechanical and non-negotiable (see next section).**

## The two blank-line rules (most important)

1. **Blank line immediately AFTER `<div dir="rtl">` and immediately BEFORE `</div>`.** Always. This guarantees markdown renders the inner content and closes the div.
2. **Blank line before AND after every code fence.** A code fence must be root-level markdown with no open RTL div above it.

Correct skeleton — copy this shape exactly:

    <div dir="rtl">

    متن یا عنوان فارسی

    </div>

    ```12:15:app/Example.php
    // code — LTR
    ```

    <div dir="rtl">

    ادامهٔ فارسی

    </div>

Note the blank line after each `<div dir="rtl">` and before each `</div>` — without them the div stays open and code goes RTL.

## Code — sacred LTR zone

Never place inside `<div dir="rtl">`, `<span dir="rtl">`, or any RTL wrapper:

- Fenced code blocks
- Code citations (`startLine:endLine:filepath`)
- Shell/command blocks
- Mermaid / ASCII diagrams

**Before typing ` ``` `:** stop, ensure the previous `<div dir="rtl">` already has its `</div>` (with a blank line before it), then add a blank line, then the fence.

Inline `` `identifier` `` inside Persian prose is fine. Paths that render badly: `<span dir="ltr">modules/Order/…</span>`.

## Persian prose, headings, lists — RTL

Put inside `<div dir="rtl">…</div>` (with the blank lines from the rule above):

- Paragraphs
- Headings (`##`, `###`, …) — including plan title/body sections after frontmatter
- Bullet and numbered lists
- Persian blockquotes

**Never** output Persian `###` or `-` lines **outside** an RTL div — they render LTR.

### What may share one RTL div

- Heading → Persian paragraph → **same** div
- Heading → Persian list → **same** div
- Anything → **code fence / mermaid** → **close the div first**, then the fence

## Plans (Plan mode / CreatePlan)

When the plan is written in Persian (or the user is working in Persian):

1. Wrap every Persian section of the plan body in `<div dir="rtl">…</div>` with the blank-line rules above.
2. Keep mermaid diagrams, code fences, and path-only technical blocks **outside** RTL divs (LTR).
3. Do **not** ship a Persian plan as bare LTR markdown headings/lists.
4. YAML frontmatter (`name`, `overview`, `todos`) may stay plain; the **plan markdown body** shown to the user must follow RTL rules for Persian text.

## Tables — renderer limitation (important)

The Cursor chat renderer wraps every table in an **LTR scroll container** and strips `style` / `align`. A markdown or raw HTML table **cannot be moved to the right edge** — `dir="rtl"` only right-aligns the *text inside cells*; the table block stays glued to the **left**. `align`, `style="margin-left:auto"`, flex containers, and raw `<table>` all fail.

**Rule:** For Persian tabular data, **do not use a markdown table** when right alignment matters. Present it as an **RTL list** instead, which right-aligns correctly:

    <div dir="rtl">

    ### وضعیت موارد

    - **بستن div قبل از کد** — درست
    - **یک div برای کل پاسخ** — ممنوع

    </div>

If a real table is unavoidable, accept the block stays left; still wrap it in `<div dir="rtl">` (with blank lines) so cell text reads RTL, and mark code/path cells with `<span dir="ltr">`. English-only / technical tables → no wrapper.

## Mixed Persian + English

Persian → RTL div. Mostly-English technical bullets → LTR, no wrapper.

## Examples

### Wrong — no blank lines inside div → div stays open → code goes RTL

    <div dir="rtl">
    ### خلاصه
    این تغییر را اعمال کردم:
    </div>
    ```12:15:app/OrderPolicy.php
    public function view(): bool
    ```

### Wrong — code fence inside the RTL div

    <div dir="rtl">

    ### خلاصه

    ```12:15:app/OrderPolicy.php
    public function view(): bool
    ```

    </div>

### Correct — blank lines inside divs, code LTR between them

    <div dir="rtl">

    ### خلاصه

    این تغییر را در `OrderPolicy.php` اعمال کردم:

    </div>

    ```12:15:app/OrderPolicy.php
    public function view(): bool
    ```

    <div dir="rtl">

    ### نتیجه

    - تست‌ها سبز شدند
    - آمادهٔ مرج است

    </div>

### Preferred — Persian tabular data as an RTL list

    <div dir="rtl">

    ### فیلدها

    - <span dir="ltr">`id`</span> — شناسه ULID
    - <span dir="ltr">`status`</span> — وضعیت رکورد

    </div>

## Pre-send checklist

- [ ] User wrote Persian or reply contains Persian → RTL applied **this turn** (not only when user reminds you).
- [ ] Every `<div dir="rtl">` has a blank line right after it and a blank line right before its `</div>`.
- [ ] Every ` ``` ` fence has a blank line before and after, and no open RTL div above it.
- [ ] No single RTL div wraps the full message or spans across a code block / mermaid.
- [ ] Persian headings and lists are inside RTL divs (not bare markdown) — including **Plan** bodies and **ops/debug** replies.
- [ ] Persian tabular data is shown as an **RTL list**, not a markdown table.
